20260529.112916.471 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.112916.471 [>kpop..........] Complete up to `10` KPOP iterations in this turn. Before beginning each iteration, write a section header `## Step K — KPOP …` to `./.malvin/logs/20260529_152109_3ajb6fp9/_kpop/exp_log_20260529_152109_3ajb6fp9_g2.md`; use the next integer K that is not already used in that file.
20260529.112916.471 [>kpop..........] 
20260529.112916.471 [>kpop..........] If you solve the problem before using the iterations budget, append a section `## KPOP_SOLVED` with one short paragraph explaining why, and stop adding new steps.
